## What changed in `/app/fixture/`

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `package.json` | Root npm manifest: `main: ./index.js`, `exports` map (`.` + `./client` + `./cordis.patch.yml` + `./package.json`), `dsh.bundle.patch → ./cordis.patch.yml`, `dsh.client = { platform: "web", inject: [] }` |
| `index.js` | Node half (moved out of `.dsh-plugin/`): empty `export function apply() {}` — gives the Loader a live host row so client-modules can scan the manifest |
| `client.js` | Browser half as a client-modules bundle: `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id: '@demo/dsh-bench-repo', factory })`, exporting `{ name, apply }`; `apply` renders the same `#bench-pet` = 🐋 element |
| `cordis.patch.yml` | Bundle layer inserting `- id: bench-pet, name: '@demo/dsh-bench-repo'` |
| `README.md` | Updated to the bundle-plugin shape |
| `.dsh-plugin/` | **Deleted** — legacy manifest, entry, and self-executing script; no `httpServer`/`tapIndex`/`/pet/ui.js`/`dsh.entry` references remain anywhere |

## Verification (dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2, isolated disposable profile)

- `dsh plugin --profile web add /app/fixture` → pnpm installed `link:/app/fixture` and reconcile appended `@demo/dsh-bench-repo` to `dsh.profile.bundles` (after `dsh-base`, `dsh-web-app`).
- `dsh --profile web --dump-config` → clean, row emitted under `# == @demo/dsh-bench-repo`, no patch warnings.
- Cold boot → `globalThis.__DSH_BOOT__` contains `{"id":"@demo/dsh-bench-repo", url:"/plugins/??@demo/dsh-bench-repo/client.js&rev=…", inject:[]}`; the bundle is served `200 text/javascript` with bytes identical to the fixture (modulo the combo trailer), and `/pet/ui.js` → **404**.
- Browser-kernel simulation: fed the real boot wire + the real served application batch into the real `dsh-client-modules` browser half; `modules.import('@demo/dsh-bench-repo')` returned `{ name, apply }` and `apply()` appended `#bench-pet` with `🐋`.

## Two environment notes (pre-existing, unrelated to the plugin)

- The session sandbox denies writes to `/root/.dsh`, so verification used an isolated `DSH_HOME` under `/tmp` (same code path).
- This container's dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2 + `cordis-plugin-hmr` has a live-patch-watch race: a **plugin-less** `web` profile fails immediately after binding with `user patch-layer watching requires the Cordis HMR service`. I confirmed it on a clean profile, then set the disposable profile's valid `patchReload: "startup"` to keep the server up for the HTTP/browser checks. The plugin itself installs, composes, and activates correctly.

